WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.712
Before writing cleaning logic, look at the raw records.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:12.602
The query on the screen selects the customer identifier, name, email, phone, address, and signup date.

00:00:12.602 --> 00:00:15.962
It then orders the records by identifier.

00:00:15.962 --> 00:00:20.252
When you run it, do not immediately start fixing values.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.086
First, look carefully.

00:00:22.558 --> 00:00:25.224
Can you see names with extra spaces?

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:28.294
Are some names capitalized differently?

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.644
Do phone numbers use different formats?

00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:35.904
Are there blank values that are different from null values?

00:00:35.904 --> 00:00:40.334
Do two rows look as if they may represent the same customer?

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:43.739
This first inspection gives you context.

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:50.049
It is similar to opening a spreadsheet and scanning the columns before writing a transformation.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:58.109
Later, we will automate much of this profiling, but visual inspection is still useful because it helps you understand

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:01.683
what kinds of problems your SQL needs to detect.
